  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the set $Y={1,6,11,16,21,26,31,36}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $Y?$\n\n$$\n{{1,16,36},{11,31},\\,____\\,}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $Y$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $Y$ and check:\n\n- $1\\in {1,16,36}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $6$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $11\\in {11,31}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $16\\in {1,16,36}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $21$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $26$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $31\\in {11,31}\\,\u2713$\n\n- $36\\in {1,16,36}\\,\u2713$\n\nThe elements $6,$ $21,$ and $26$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${6,21,26}.$",
